       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given in divided doses. Extended-release is limited to 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. This order is about twice that limit.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which is the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** If so, tell me the intended dose and frequency, and whether the formulation is immediate-release or extended-release.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please tell me the clinical rationale. I can add it as a note, though I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
